{"items":[{"str":"now lit with a shaft of light from a window broken in the struggle. First,","dir":"ltr","width":288,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,156,649],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"there’s a medium shot of a child’s size American flag leaning against a","dir":"ltr","width":288,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,156,636],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"dusty army helmet and then a close-up of a sea-blue paper mobile with a","dir":"ltr","width":288,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,156,623],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"butterfly design—a bit of Chinatown interior decoration or a trophy","dir":"ltr","width":288,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,156,610],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"from Viet Nam. Bill’s inheritance and his legacy. Which is why the final","dir":"ltr","width":288,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,156,597],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"image of Lecter after his murderous escape, sauntering down a crowded","dir":"ltr","width":288,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,156,584],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"main street in Haiti [","dir":"ltr","width":86,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,156,571],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"sic","dir":"ltr","width":9,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,242,571],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":false},{"str":"] resplendent in his creamy tourist suit, is more","dir":"ltr","width":192,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,252,571],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"disturbing than anything that has come before. The serial killer, an","dir":"ltr","width":288,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,156,558],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"American gift to the third world, a fragmentation bomb, ready to ex-","dir":"ltr","width":288,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,156,545],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"plode. (16)","dir":"ltr","width":46,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,156,532],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"Taubin’s interpretation brings into view a possibly progressive, politi-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,144,509],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"cal reading of this film. This is what is meant by the term","dir":"ltr","width":262,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,144,494],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":" ","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,406,494],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"disavowal","dir":"ltr","width":46,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,410,494],"fontName":"g_d2896_f1","hasEOL":false},{"str":"","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,144,480],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"and how it functions: one knows that something is true, but one re-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,144,480],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"fuses that knowledge and constructs a cover story for that which one","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,144,466],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"refuses to know. Thus one both knows and does not know “the","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,144,452],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"truth.” To foreground disavowal as a structure within representation","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,144,438],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"allows us to identify and discuss this recognition of institutionalized","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,144,424],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"violence in our culture and makes it possible to link stories of individ-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,144,410],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"ualized pathology to the social.","dir":"ltr","width":139,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,144,396],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[9,0,0,9,204,677],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":true},{"str":"Cultural Studies, Popular Culture, and Pedagogy","dir":"ltr","width":191,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,204,677],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":false},{"str":"","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[9,0,0,9,287,117],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"| 31 |","dir":"ltr","width":26,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,287,117],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false}],"styles":{"g_d2896_f2":{"fontFamily":"serif","ascent":0.722,"descent":-0.246,"vertical":false},"g_d2896_f3":{"fontFamily":"serif","ascent":0.722,"descent":-0.246,"vertical":false},"g_d2896_f1":{"fontFamily":"serif","ascent":0.72,"descent":-0.245,"vertical":false}},"lang":null}